WHY SHARE-ALIKE AND NOT PUBLIC DOMAIN
    Strictly, the facts here -- who dated whom, in which episode -- are probably
    not copyrightable, and under US law (Feist) a database of them would not be
    protected on effort alone. Share-alike is therefore the courteous answer
    rather than the minimum defensible one: the source is BY-SA, the selection
    and arrangement is where the work went, and mirroring the licence keeps the
    obligation flowing the way the wiki's contributors intended.
